            <ArticleTitle>[Large stump of the cystic duct].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>56-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors concluded that a large stump of the gall-bladder duct is of no independent importance as a cause of the affection. However, concretions may be formed in the stump, that was evident in three cases, therefore, the gall duct stump should be no more than 0.5 cm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
